the text of "the L4 source module-5-examples.l4" is at "sources/module-5-examples.l4".

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the clock reaches day the day from the time to the second time.

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    a party does deliver the goods on day the day from the time to the second time.

a party does something on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the party does deliver the goods on day the day from the time to the second time.

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    a party does pay the invoice with amount an amount on day the day from the time to the second time.

a party does something on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the party does pay the invoice with amount an amount on day the day from the time to the second time.

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    a party does exchange vows on day the day from the time to the second time.

a party does something on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the party does exchange vows on day the day from the time to the second time.

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    a party does be unfaithful on day the day from the time to the second time.

a party does something on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the party does be unfaithful on day the day from the time to the second time.

something happens on day a day from a time to a second time if
    a party does cancel the order on day the day from the time to the second time.

a party does something on day a day from a time to a second time if
    the party does cancel the order on day the day from the time to the second time.

% The contract the delivery obligation starts: its first obligations.
when the contract the delivery obligation starts on day a day
    and a due day = day + 14
then the delivery obligation obliges the_seller to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The contract the complete sale contract starts: its first obligations.
when the contract the complete sale contract starts on day a day
    and a due day = day + 14
then the complete sale contract obliges the_seller to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The contract the payment with late fee starts: its first obligations.
when the contract the payment with late fee starts on day a day
    and a due day = day + 30
then the payment with late fee obliges the_buyer to pay the invoice with amount 1000 by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The contract the wedding ceremony starts: its first obligations.
when the contract the wedding ceremony starts on day a day
    and a due day = day + 1
then the wedding ceremony obliges spouse_1 to exchange vows by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The contract the fidelity clause starts: its first obligations.
when the contract the fidelity clause starts on day a day
then the fidelity clause forbids spouse_1 to be unfaithful as its first obligation.

% The first obligation of the delivery obligation: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does deliver the goods on day a day
    and the delivery obligation obliges the party to deliver the goods by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day <= the due day
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the delivery obligation obliges the party to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the delivery obligation obliges a party to deliver the goods by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the contract is breached
    and it is not the case that the delivery obligation obliges the party to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The first obligation of the complete sale contract: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does deliver the goods on day a day
    and the complete sale contract obliges the party to deliver the goods by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day <= the due day
    and a second due day = day + 30
then the complete sale contract obliges the_buyer to pay the invoice with amount 1000 by day the second due day as its second obligation
    and it is not the case that the complete sale contract obliges the party to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the complete sale contract obliges a party to deliver the goods by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the complete sale contract permits the_seller to cancel the order as its third obligation
    and it is not the case that the complete sale contract obliges the party to deliver the goods by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The first obligation of the payment with late fee: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does pay the invoice with amount an amount on day a day
    and the payment with late fee obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day <= the due day
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the payment with late fee obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day the due day as its first obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the payment with late fee obliges a party to pay the invoice with amount an amount by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day > the due day
    and a second due day = day + 14
then the payment with late fee obliges the_buyer to pay the invoice with amount 1100 by day the second due day as its second obligation
    and it is not the case that the payment with late fee obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The first obligation of the wedding ceremony: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does exchange vows on day a day
    and the wedding ceremony obliges the party to exchange vows by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day <= the due day
    and a second due day = day + 1
then the wedding ceremony obliges spouse_2 to exchange vows by day the second due day as its second obligation
    and it is not the case that the wedding ceremony obliges the party to exchange vows by day the due day as its first obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the wedding ceremony obliges a party to exchange vows by day a due day as its first obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the contract is breached by spouse_1 because "failed to exchange vows"
    and it is not the case that the wedding ceremony obliges the party to exchange vows by day the due day as its first obligation.

% The first obligation of the fidelity clause: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does be unfaithful on day a day
    and the fidelity clause forbids the party to be unfaithful as its first obligation
then the contract is breached by spouse_1 because "was unfaithful"
    and it is not the case that the fidelity clause forbids the party to be unfaithful as its first obligation.

% The second obligation of the complete sale contract: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does pay the invoice with amount an amount on day a day
    and the complete sale contract obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day a due day as its second obligation
    and the day <= the due day
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the complete sale contract obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day the due day as its second obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the complete sale contract obliges a party to pay the invoice with amount an amount by day a due day as its second obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the contract is breached
    and it is not the case that the complete sale contract obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day the due day as its second obligation.

% The third obligation of the complete sale contract: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does cancel the order on day a day
    and the complete sale contract permits the party to cancel the order as its third obligation
then the contract is breached
    and it is not the case that the complete sale contract permits the party to cancel the order as its third obligation.

% The second obligation of the payment with late fee: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does pay the invoice with amount an amount on day a day
    and the payment with late fee obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day a due day as its second obligation
    and the day <= the due day
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the payment with late fee obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day the due day as its second obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the payment with late fee obliges a party to pay the invoice with amount an amount by day a due day as its second obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the contract is breached
    and it is not the case that the payment with late fee obliges the party to pay the invoice with amount the amount by day the due day as its second obligation.

% The second obligation of the wedding ceremony: met, or its deadline missed.
when a party does exchange vows on day a day
    and the wedding ceremony obliges the party to exchange vows by day a due day as its second obligation
    and the day <= the due day
then the contract is fulfilled
    and it is not the case that the wedding ceremony obliges the party to exchange vows by day the due day as its second obligation.

when something happens on day a day
    and the wedding ceremony obliges a party to exchange vows by day a due day as its second obligation
    and the day > the due day
then the contract is breached by spouse_2 because "failed to exchange vows"
    and it is not the case that the wedding ceremony obliges the party to exchange vows by day the due day as its second obligation.

